---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const title = "West Covina City Hall Updates | StayJustIn";
const description =
  "West Covina City Hall news, council meeting updates, Fire Station 3 emergency repairs, City Yard redevelopment, budget questions, public safety costs, and local government decisions explained simply.";
---

<MainLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://www.stayjustin.com/city-hall/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="page-kicker">West Covina City Hall</p>
        <h1>City Hall Decisions Residents Should Watch</h1>
        <p>
          West Covina is dealing with emergency repairs, redevelopment talks,
          labor agreements, budget pressure, and procedural decisions that can
          shape the city long before residents see a final vote.
        </p>
        <p>
          This page brings together the most important City Hall stories so residents
          can follow what is being approved, what questions still need answers,
          and how decisions may affect the city budget, neighborhoods, and public services.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="featured-card">
        <span class="featured-badge">Featured Story</span>
        <h2>
          <a href="/city-hall/what-residents-miss-city-council-meetings/">
            What Residents Often Miss During West Covina City Council Meetings
          </a>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Emergency resolutions, AB 1234 reports, City Yard negotiations, council
          requests, and budget signals are often buried in procedural sections many
          residents skip.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more-link" href="/city-hall/what-residents-miss-city-council-meetings/">
          Read the full breakdown →
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Related City Hall Stories</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">The newest issues residents should be watching.</p>

    <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/athens-services-west-covina-trash-contract-rate-increases-2048/">
  <span>Trash Rates</span>
  <strong>Athens Services contract, rate increases, and 2048 lock-in explained</strong>
  <p>How West Covina’s long-term waste agreement affects residents, businesses, enforcement, and city leverage.</p>
</a>

      <div class="compact-card-grid">
        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/fire-station-3-emergency-repairs-continue/">
          <span>Fire Station 3</span>
          <strong>Emergency repairs continue under special authority</strong>
          <p>Why emergency status matters for costs, bidding, contractor work, and accountability.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/april-21-2026-city-council-budget-questions/">
          <span>Budget Watch</span>
          <strong>Budget questions residents should be asking right now</strong>
          <p>Emergency spending, overtime, labor costs, and budget assumptions all connect.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-overtime-spending-analysis/">
          <span>Overtime</span>
          <strong>Overtime spending is already over 50% at mid-year</strong>
          <p>Police and fire overtime are key numbers residents should watch.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-q2-financial-report-2025-26/">
          <span>Budget</span>
          <strong>West Covina Q2 financial report explained</strong>
          <p>Revenue timing may explain part of the gap, but pressure still matters.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-fire-management-mou-2024-2028/">
          <span>Labor</span>
          <strong>Fire Management MOU: what it costs over time</strong>
          <p>A new agreement creates future public safety labor costs through 2028.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/development/west-covina-city-yard-brandywine-project/">
          <span>City Yard</span>
          <strong>City Yard / Brandywine redevelopment explained</strong>
          <p>The ENA vote is not final approval, but it can shape future redevelopment negotiations.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">How We Got Here</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Background coverage connecting the larger City Hall story.</p>

      <div class="compact-card-grid">
        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-city-hall-investigation/">
          <span>Investigation</span>
          <strong>What’s happening at West Covina City Hall?</strong>
          <p>A full breakdown of ongoing issues, decisions, and concerns shaping City Hall activity.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-city-hall-timeline/">
          <span>Timeline</span>
          <strong>West Covina City Hall timeline</strong>
          <p>A step-by-step timeline showing how key events unfolded.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-code-of-conduct-censure-explained/">
          <span>Policy</span>
          <strong>Code of Conduct explained: how censure works</strong>
          <p>What censure means in West Covina and why the process matters.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-gutierrez-censure/">
          <span>Censure</span>
          <strong>Why Brian Gutierrez was censured</strong>
          <p>What led to the censure decision and how it connects to broader City Hall dynamics.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">More City Hall Coverage</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Older stories residents can review for background and context.</p>

      <div class="compact-card-grid">
        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-fire-station-3-emergency-repairs/">
          <span>Fire Department</span>
          <strong>West Covina Fire Station 3 emergency repairs proposed</strong>
          <p>Earlier coverage of the Fire Station 3 repair issue.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-lawsuits-fire-chief/">
          <span>Lawsuits</span>
          <strong>West Covina lawsuits and fire chief controversy explained</strong>
          <p>Background on legal issues and public safety leadership questions.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="topic-story-card" href="/city-hall/west-covina-moon-festival-spending/">
          <span>Public Spending</span>
          <strong>West Covina Moon Festival spending overview</strong>
          <p>A look at public spending questions tied to the Moon Festival discussion.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
